<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7744" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Chărĭsĭus</span></b> ,
			ĭi, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χαρίσιος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Greek orator</i>, <i>imitator of
				Lysias</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut. 83, 286</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 10,
				1, 70</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Flavius Sosipater Charisius, <i>a Latin
				grammarian in the fourth Christian
			century.</i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A Roman jurist of the time of Constantine the
			Great.</i>
		</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
